      <direction placement="above">
        <direction-type>
          <words default-x="-21.00" default-y="328.03" valign="top" font-size="12">This waltz is in what I would consider to be a Quasi-Sonata Form. It isn't your typical Sonata Form, but it is quite similar
</words>
          <words>to Sonata Form. The first A section you could consider to be the Exposition, the B section and Digression, you could 
</words>
          <words>consider both to be part of the Development section, and the second A section, you could consider to be the Recapitulation.
</words>
          <words>
</words>
          <words>Or you could just say that the waltz is in an atypical Ternary Form and leave it at that. Either way you look at it, it isn't in a
</words>
          <words>typical form for the genre. I personally would describe this as a Quasi-Sonata Form though, because of the significance of
</words>
          <words>each section and each theme in each section, including the Coda.
</words>
          <words />
        </direction-type>
      </direction>
